  "note": "Maps each recorded fact scripts/fact-inventory.ts finds (74 today) to (a) an existing test file with round-trip coverage of it, and whether that coverage is a DEDICATED lemma test (the printer writes bytes from which the reader re-derives the fact, and reverting the recording reds that test) rather than an ordinary round-trip that happens to exercise it (landedLemma), and (b) the tests/conformance/reparse-ledger.json families it explains, with a basis. 'measured' is the strongest and the rarest: the fact's own lemma is red-detectable AND re-running the reparse measurement over the whole population moves that family's rows and no others. 'argued' means the family's written mechanism and the fact's written purpose name the same thing, with nobody having traced a row; it counts toward the scoreboard. 'argued-not-counted' is a connection considered and rejected as too thematic to count, recorded rather than dropped silently. The legal values are the closed list in scripts/fact-inventory.ts (FACT_BASES), and ledgerFailures there rejects any other. reparseFamilySizes MIRRORS the live reparse ledger, family by family, and ledgerFailures holds it there in both directions - so a family a fix has EMPTIED reads 0 rather than losing its key. Read the scoreboard with that in mind: the attribution percentage the 50% retirement gate was pre-registered against was taken over the population as it stood when the census landed (276 rows, of which blank-dropped held 70), and a fact whose family now reads 0 is a fact that did its job rather than one that explains nothing.",
